  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Adds CC032: flags a Task/ValueTask-returning call whose result is discarded in non-async code. This fills a real compiler gap — CS4014 only fires inside an async method, so a constructor, a synchronous method, or a non-async lambda gets no warning at all, and a dropped task cannot be cancelled, awaited at shutdown, or have its failure observed. Conservative: tasks that are assigned, returned, passed as arguments, or explicitly discarded with _ = are not flagged, and CC032 stays quiet wherever CS4014 already reports. Analyzer-only, because the right resolution depends on intent. 32 diagnostics.",
